          {
            "commit": "0f6b84d57edfb463934ca3333366ca0785756ba3",
            "subject": "LU-18298 pcc: purge page cache before removing a PCC copy"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-08 03:08:18.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-09 03:07:20.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-18298 pcc: pick up a lapsed copy in the detach ioctl",
        "message": "LU-18298 pcc: pick up a lapsed copy in the detach ioctl\n\npcc_ioctl_detach() returns success without removing the HSM archive\nwhen the client has no PCC inode attached, even though the copy is\nstill valid on the backend. \"lfs pcc detach -k\" leaves exactly that.\n\nIt has always relied on the caller having opened the file first, so\nthat pcc_file_open() re-attached it. Do that same PIT_OPEN attach in\nthe ioctl instead, under the dataset gating open uses, so no layout\nis refreshed and no lock is taken.\n\nThe next patch stops lfs pcc detach opening the file at all, which\nis what makes sanity-pcc test_16 depend on this.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nFixes: 2dadefb4148f (\"LU-10092 pcc: change detach behavior and add keep option\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I617ccd6fb847a6b368b4b107fb0fc9fc8ffae00f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
